# Elixir runtime

Work from `runtime/`. The HTTP table is `runtime/README.md`. This process orchestrates IPFS and IOTA Identity; the UI stays in Godot (ADR 0003).

- Format changed files with `mix format`.
- Run the matching test file, for example `mix test test/concrete_runtime_bootstrap_test.exs`. Run `mix test` when the change crosses modules.
- A mutating route checks a capability before it writes. On denial, respond `403` with `%{error: "capability_denied"}`, as `POST /v1/identity` does in `lib/concrete_runtime/api.ex`.

```elixir
case ConcreteRuntime.Bootstrap.authorize(principal_id, "mutate") do
  {:ok, _, _} ->
    # publish, then send_json(conn, 201, created)
    :ok

  {:error, :capability_denied} ->
    send_json(conn, 403, %{error: "capability_denied"})
end
```
